{
  "id": 304238771,
  "iid": 15738,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "MySQL: Assume MYSQL_CAPS_DE if we don't have clnt_caps_ext",
  "description": "If the capture is missing the login packet it doesn't know which capabilities are set. For both MySQL and MariaDB the best guess is that `MYSQL_CAPS_DE` (aka `DEPRECATE_EOF`) is set.\n\nThe result of this is that 'incomplete' conversations with somewhat recent MySQL and MariaDB should work fine. However 'incomplete' conversations from older MySQL/MariaDB versions that don't set this flag won't work.\n\nCloses #19851 \n\nSee also:\n- https://dev.mysql.com/worklog/task/?id=7766",
  "state": "closed",
