  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "3c763fb3328562f66b1ad4597ba3ccaa252ecae2",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1921896973,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Aren't there several other places where `MYSQL_CAPS_DE` is checked? Should it be assumed everywhere?\n\nShould this be a preference, if it can't be auto-detected?\n\nIt looks like the biggest difference is when after all the field packets are sent, whether an intermediate EOF is sent before the row packets. Currently, when all the field packets are sent, if the intermediate EOF is expected the state stays in `FIELD_PACKET` and handles the EOF there, even though it knows there are no more field packets expected.\n\nIs it possible to introduce a new state, or otherwise handle it with the number of expected field packets left, such that a packet is interpreted an intermediate EOF if an EOF but a row packet if not? Currently it's interpreted as a final EOF or row packet in the ROW PACKET state, or as an intermediate EOF or field packet in the FIELD PACKET state, neither of which work.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-05-25T11:05:05.734Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-05-25T11:05:05.734Z",
